      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 30 mg is three times the maximum recommended dose, which is 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg. Doses that high raise the risk of severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdose can also cause prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function and a 70 kg weight don't change that ceiling.\n\nWhich of these do you want?\n- **10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n- **A different dose**, such as 5 mg PO once daily, or 2.5 mg if you want to start low.\n- **30 mg as written**, if it's intentional. Tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose.\n\nIf the goal is more blood pressure control than 10 mg gives, I can enter amlodipine at a standard dose. You could then add another agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic, and I can enter that order too."
      }
     ],
